WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.586
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:09.586 --> 00:00:15.886
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:15.886 --> 00:00:24.686
Napoleon | Capture scoring cards
Each ace, king, queen and jack is worth one point: 16 total. Count scoring cards, not tricks.

00:00:24.686 --> 00:00:31.886
This four-player example enables joker summons. Napoleon and the secretary win by reaching the bid; everyone else defends.

00:00:31.886 --> 00:00:41.786
Bid for target and trump
North bids 9 hearts; everyone passes. Hearts are trumps and Napoleon’s side needs nine scoring cards.

00:00:41.786 --> 00:00:49.886
Bid levels run from 9 to 16. Raise the bid or pass. All passes redeal; there is no weak-hand redeal request.

00:00:49.886 --> 00:00:59.786
Take the kitty and discard
In a four-player game, take two kitty cards and discard two. North discards the club two and three.

00:00:59.786 --> 00:01:07.886
Other players acknowledge the public discards. Any discarded ace, king, queen or jack scores for the defenders.

00:01:07.886 --> 00:01:19.886
Acknowledge the discards
Each other player must acknowledge. Wait for them; no further card selection is needed here.

00:01:19.886 --> 00:01:29.786
Name the secretary card
North names the spade ace. Its holder is the hidden secretary; North cannot see who holds it yet.

00:01:29.786 --> 00:01:37.886
Only the holder knows their role until the card is played. Naming your own or a discarded card can leave Napoleon playing alone.

00:01:37.886 --> 00:01:48.886
Trump two summons the big joker
North leads the heart two, forcing the big joker. Watch for the secretary card; its holder becomes known only when it is played.

00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:57.886
Normally follow suit, but jokers and the secretary card may be played anytime. A valid summon forces its holder to respond.

00:01:57.886 --> 00:02:06.686
Secretary beats the big joker
East’s secretary ace wins two scoring cards. Winning one trick need not mean earning one point.

00:02:06.686 --> 00:02:13.886
Normally: secretary card > big joker > small joker > trump > led suit. Compare rank within a class. The winner leads next.

00:02:13.886 --> 00:03:29.886
Finish the deal | Repeated plays accelerated
Watch the aces, kings, queens and jacks captured each trick. Both sides must total 16 scoring cards.

00:03:29.886 --> 00:03:39.786
Essential exception | Last three tricks
Rule explanation: this example has no jokers in its final three tricks.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:47.886
Jokers become weakest in the final three tricks; the secretary remains strongest. Leading a joker or secretary card requires selecting a led suit.

00:03:47.886 --> 00:03:58.886
Essential exception | Summons and options
Rule explanation: check the room options before play.

00:03:58.886 --> 00:04:07.886
With joker summons enabled, leading trump two summons the big joker; trump three summons the small joker. Napoleon may request the secretary when leading, provided the lead does not also trigger a joker summon. NT has no automatic joker summons.

00:04:07.886 --> 00:04:17.786
Result | Combine teammates’ points
Napoleon and the secretary have 13 points, beating their target of nine. The defenders have three.

00:04:17.786 --> 00:05:01.382
Five/six-player games have different kitty sizes and private discards until settlement, with no public-discard acknowledgement. See detailed rules for variants.
